{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>I walk to my people.</b> From now on I am like the rest of my people — the Holy One, blessed be He, has withdrawn from him." "<b>Come, I will advise you.</b> What should you do, and what is the counsel? Their god of these — he hates immorality, etc., as is found in Ḥelek (Sanhedrin 106); know that Bilaam gave this counsel to make them stumble through immorality, for behold it is stated: ״הֵן הֵנָּה הָיוּ לִבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל בִּדְבַר בִּלְעָם״ (Numbers 31)." "<b>What this people will do to your people.</b> This is an elliptical verse: 'I will advise you to make them stumble, and I will tell you what they are destined to do evil to Moav in the end of days' — ״וּמָחַץ פַּאֲתֵי מוֹאָב״; the Targum spells out what the Hebrew leaves elliptical."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {1 "Reading אֱלֹהֵיהֶם, 'their god,' as the text stands; the reference is to the God of Israel."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:37.155089756Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}